When the core and the project tier resolve to one directory — a vault in the plugin root whose
`vault/specs` is also configured as the core tier — a targeted rule injects once, under the core
tier's ref. The plugin root is the real checkout, so the vault's config points the core tier at the
sandbox repo's `vault/specs`, the directory the project tier's null `path` resolves to.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/config.yaml --
core:
  specs:
    tiers:
      core: {path: ~/../cwd/vault}
      project: {path: null}
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/rule/0001-shared-rule.md --
---
type: rule
title: Shared rule
status: accepted
targets: [fx-rule-shared]
brief: Shared brief.
---
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/_playbooks/fx-rule-shared/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-rule-shared
title: Rules
summary: Rule injection.
---

Preamble.
